d mash the garlic. It should equal 1 tablespoon. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Put the white potatoes and sweet potato in a large pot, cover with water, add the 2 teaspoons of salt and boil until the potatoes are tender, about 30 minutes, and drain in a colander."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Place the hot potatoes in a large bowl. Add the garlic, butter and milk and, using a hand mixer, whip the potatoes until very smooth. Add the black pepper and adjust the seasoning with additional salt and pepper to taste. Serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 412.1, "protein_g": 6.2, "carbohydrates_g": 44.8, "fat_g": 24.2, "saturated_fat_g": 15.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 64.1, "sodium_mg": 509.8, "fiber_g": 5.3, "sugar_g": 4.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["southern"], "diet": [], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": ["christmas"], "other": ["boil", "five ingredient", "roast", "russet potato", "sweet potato", "winter"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1996-12-22", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T03:21:18.392191+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "ammonia-cookies", "nyt_id": 1727, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1727-ammonia-cookies", "name": "Ammonia Cookies", "author": "Dena Kleiman", "description": "Jenan Madden, the manager of a book store in Seattle, shared this recipe with The Times. She acquired it as a child from a favorite baby sitter. “The taste is great,” she said. “And it’s fun telling people what they are called.” (Ammonia cookies are in fact made with ammonium carbonate, a form of baking soda, not cleaning ammonia, which is poisonous.) Dena Kleiman", "servings": {"text": "48 cookies", "min": 48, "max": 48, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup butter, at room temperature", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "butter", "preparation": "at room temperature", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 cup solid vegetable shortening", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "solid vegetable shortening", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 ½ cups sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 cup shredded coconut", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "shredded coconut", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 cups flour", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 teaspoons baking ammonia, crushed (see note)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "baking ammonia", "preparation": "crushed (see note)", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees."}, {"position": 2, "tex